For HubSpot single-send API customProperties, you'll access them directly as top-level variables in your HubL template:

```hubl
{# Print the order total #}
<p>Order Total: ${{ order_total }}</p>

{# Conditional members-only block #}
{% if is_member %}
<div class="members-only">
  <h2>Thanks for being a member!</h2>
  <p>Enjoy your exclusive member benefits...</p>
</div>
{% endif %}
```

**Key points:**
- customProperties from the API payload are accessed directly by name (`{{ order_total }}`, not `{{ contact.order_total }}`)
- Use `{% if is_member %}` for the conditional block (HubL treats boolean true as truthy)
- Make sure your API call sends the properties with matching names

**Example API payload structure:**
```json
{
  "emailId": 12345,
  "message": {
    "to": "customer@example.com"
  },
  "customProperties": {
    "order_total": "49.99",
    "is_member": true
  }
}
```

If you need to format the order total as currency or handle edge cases (like missing values), you can add HubL filters:

```hubl
<p>Order Total: ${{ order_total|format_number("0.00") }}</p>
```

